==============================================================================
(1) GAUSSIAN ONSET FROM A STATE-INDEPENDENT RAMPING SEAL  lambda(t)=a t
==============================================================================
  Claim (paper56 sec.3, C12): a state-independent irreversible seal with
  hazard lambda(t)=a t gives |rho01(T)| = exp(-INT_0^T lambda) = exp(-a T^2/2),
  reproducing Paper X's Gaussian onset EXACTLY (so the Gaussian shape is
  NOT itself a non-Markovian / state-dependent signature).
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SYMBOLIC (sympy):
    INT_0^T (a t) dt                         = T**2*a/2
    |rho01(T)| = exp(-INT lambda)            = exp(-T**2*a/2)
    target exp(-a T^2/2) - |rho01(T)|        = 0   (exact 0 => identity holds)
    d/dT ln|rho01| at T=0 (zero-slope plateau)= 0   (=0 => quadratic onset)
    constant hazard lambda0 instead          => |rho01| = exp(-lambda0 T)  (pure exponential semigroup)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
