  T= 7.0:  exp(-INT lam) vs exp(-aT^2/2)         = 0.00000000002289734845645552894085224694165523418863   [resid 0.0]

==============================================================================
(2) OU (EXPONENTIAL) KERNEL IS CP-DIVISIBLE   K(s)=sigma^2 e^{-|s|/tau_c}
==============================================================================
  Running integral  I(T)=INT_0^T K = sigma^2 tau_c (1 - e^{-T/tau_c}) >= 0,
  dephasing rate    gamma(T)=2 chi'(T)=(2 sigma^2 tau_c/hbar^2)(1-e^{-T/tau_c}) >= 0
  for ALL T  =>  CP-divisible (RHP/BLP-Markovian, no revivals); |C(T)| monotone.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SYMBOLIC (sympy):
    I(T)=INT_0^T K                 = sigma**2*tau_c - sigma**2*tau_c*exp(-T/tau_c)
    I(T) - sigma^2 tau_c (1-e^-T/tc)= 0   (exact 0)
