==============================================================================
(5) OU-NOISE vs SPARSE-SEAL: BIT-IDENTICAL TO ALL ORDERS
==============================================================================
  Continuous OU dephasing:  C_OU(T) = exp[-chi(T)],
    chi(T) = (sigma^2 tau_c^2/hbar^2)(T/tau_c - 1 + e^{-T/tau_c}).
  State-independent irreversible seal with hazard
    lambda_OU(t)=chi'(t)=(sigma^2 tau_c/hbar^2)(1 - e^{-t/tau_c}):
    C_seal(T) = exp[-INT_0^T lambda_OU] = exp[-chi(T)]   (since chi(0)=0).
  => |C_OU(T) - C_seal(T)| = 0 to ALL orders: the two mechanisms are
     OPERATIONALLY UNDECIDABLE from the reduced channel.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SYMBOLIC (sympy):
    chi'(T)                         = sigma**2*tau_c*(exp(T/tau_c) - 1)*exp(-T/tau_c)/hbar**2
    lambda_OU(T)                    = sigma**2*tau_c*(exp(T/tau_c) - 1)*exp(-T/tau_c)/hbar**2
    chi'(T) - lambda_OU(T)          = 0   (exact 0)
    INT_0^T lambda_OU - chi(T)      = 0   (exact 0 => all-orders identity)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
