(6) BIMODAL LIMIT  delta E = +/- sigma_E  =>  C(T)=cos(sigma_E T/hbar)
==============================================================================
  In the long-memory regime C(T)=<exp(i deltaE T/hbar)>. A symmetric two-point
  (branch-selecting) delta E = +/- sigma_E gives a NON-Gaussian, REVIVING
  coherence cos(sigma_E T/hbar) that no monotone exp[-chi] can produce.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SYMBOLIC (sympy):
    C(T) = (1/2)(e^{i sigma_E T/hbar} + e^{-i sigma_E T/hbar}) = cos(T*sigma_E/hbar)
    C(T) - cos(sigma_E T/hbar)            = 0   (exact 0)
